<!-- Install Switch: the one Shortcut a queue of This iPhone installs runs before and after (LocalVPN.runSwitch).
     Its input is a JSON dictionary of flags, read with Get Dictionary Value and tested with "has any value" only
     (B359: a "contains" condition loses its text on import):
       {"start":1[,"cellular":1]}  remember the VPN that is on now (Store Content "previous VPN"), then Set VPN: connect
                                   the built-in VPN (Find VPNs, server 10.7.0.1), then Cellular Data Off when
                                   "cellular" (sent only by app builds before B375; this one sends dataOff)
       {"dataOff":1}               Cellular Data Off: the app runs it once the built-in VPN is connected. B375: iOS
                                   starts no VPN without a network ("No network available"), so data goes off only
                                   after the VPN is up; an open VPN stays up without it (SideStore's order)
       {"end":1[,"cellular":1]}    Cellular Data On when "cellular", then Set VPN: connect the remembered VPN, forgotten
       {"check":1}                 nothing: the app's check run after Add; with "actions":1 one Wait for Install
       {"trip":1[,"cellular":1]}   F394, iOS 16+: all of it in one run. Remember the VPN, Connect VPN (the app's action),
                                   Cellular Data Off when "cellular", Open for Install (the app in front), Wait for
                                   Install until the queue is over, Cellular Data On, Set VPN back
     The VPN to bring back isn't chosen at Add (no import question): the start's Store Content keeps whichever VPN
     was on, a VPN object (R76: text can't become a VPN), so the user picks nothing.
     tools/shortcuts/sign.sh signs it. Set VPN keys: journal/2026-11-23-f386-install-switch. -->
